For the final assignment we were asked to code something of our own. I decided to code a game, "Flyscape". Flyscape is the combination of two words, fly and escape. In the game, the fly would try to escape predators inside a forest. The forest would start away from the user and the come closer and eventually disappearing out of the screen, thus creating the illusion of depth. The movement of the fly is to be controlled the movement of the cursor. For this I created two images of the fly to create a wings flapping motion. Along with that, three leaf designs witha ahole in the center, through which the fly will move. the three leaf designs will appear one behind the other randomly infinitely. The predators are three, and each of them had three sprites. THey will also appear randomly from random angles to catch the fly. This project turned out to be a reality check on how difficult it is to code a simple game like this. I've understood that it is tough to learn Javacsript coding in 2 weeks for me. To understand the logic of the game it took me a while, so the coding also lagged. Coding the fly was easy, I created a class, and made the changes there, restricted the fly's movement to mouseX and mouseY. But, the real problems came when the leaves had to move towards the user and scaling up at the same time. I created a leaves class, loaded the images, but the images were not scaling up properly. Then to solve this a loop was used to solve the issue. A class predators were created to introduce the hunters to the game. At last, the collision, a function was added in the fly class to check collision whenever the fly reaches too close to the predator. The game is still not a final product, it is a work in progress, as it is not exactly as I imagined it, but still works.
